meta { name: Refusal — forged consumer header, type: http, seq: 6 }
get { url: {{publicBase}}/articles/{{sharedSlug}}, body: none, auth: none }
headers {
  X-Tenant-Key: {{gamingTenantKey}}
  X-Consumer-Custom-ID: 0198f000-0000-7000-8000-000000000001
}
docs {
  A valid GAMING key plus a forged technology tenant id in X-Consumer-Custom-ID.
  Kong overwrites X-Consumer-* rather than appending, so this must return the
  GAMING article. If it returns the technology one, the gateway is not stripping
  client-supplied consumer headers and any tenant can read any other.

  This is the test that backs the "verified, not assumed" claim in kong.yml.
}
